  "Onderdeel: uitklap Geavanceerd": "Component: Advanced foldout",
  "The Advanced foldout": "",
  "The menu shows the work. Everything an agent needs now and then, and everything that sets the app up, waits one click away under Advanced, the last entry in the sidebar footer. It opens in place, under the entry, and pushes nothing else away. \"Modules and more\" used to be a menu entry of its own; on Ruben's decision it moved out of the menu into this foldout, where it is now called Modules.": "",
  "What the foldout holds, and where each entry comes from": "",
  "Entry": "",
  "Why it is here": "",
  "Source": "",
  "Reports": "",
  "Looked at now and then, not worked from. Reporting, Contact reporting, Channel analytics, Agent performance, Forecast, Loyalty and SLA attainment are cards on this one page.": "",
  "Manifest, settings section. Seven reports removed from the menu point here.": "",
  "Automation that runs by itself once it is set up.": "",
  "Manifest, settings section": "",
  "Module pages": "",
  "The pages of a module that is on, such as Point of sale, Contracts, Prospects, Contacts and the marketing tools. They open from here, never as extra entries in the daily menu.": "",
  "Modules page, one entry per module": "",
  "The stages a lead or request moves through. Set once, changed rarely.": "",
  "Menu layout, settings section": "",
  "Services and Resources": "Services and resources",
  "What can be booked and who or what it is booked on. The bookings themselves stay under Appointments.": "",
  "Simple menu layout, settings section": "",
  "Integrations and BI export": "",
  "Connections to other systems and the export for business intelligence.": "",
  "Sales, Marketing, Point of Sale, Products, Contracts and Loyalty, for teams that use them.": "Sales, Marketing, Point of sale, Products, Contracts and Loyalty, for teams that use them.",
  "Simple menu layout, modules": "",
  "Store, Features and roadmap": "",
  "About the app, not about the work: what can be added and what is coming.": "",
  "Manifest, footer section": "",
  "Full menu, Admin settings": "",
  "Only an administrator sees these. Admin settings opens the Nextcloud admin page for Pipelinq.": "",
  "Admin page, Menu structure": "",
  "What belongs in Advanced": "",
  "Configuration a team sets up once and then leaves alone: pipelines, bookable services and resources, connections.": "",
  "Overviews that are read, not worked from: every report sits on the one Reports page.": "",
  "Automation that runs without a person: flows.": "",
  "Things about the app rather than the work: the store, features and roadmap.": "",
  "The switch back to the full menu, and the way to the admin page, for administrators only.": "",
  "What never goes in Advanced": "",
  "Anything an agent works from every day: questions and reports, contact moments, appointments, residents and businesses, My work, the Queue.": "",
  "A primary action. New request stays at the top of the sidebar.": "",
  "Help. It is the first footer entry and always one click away.": "",
  "Settings that change the instance, such as message providers, telephony and payment providers. Those live on the Nextcloud admin page; Advanced only links to it.": "",
  "A page that exists nowhere else. Everything in Advanced is also reachable by its own link, and the full menu shows it again.": "",
  "Switching the full menu back on": "",
  "Pipelinq opens with the simple menu. Nothing is removed: both menus open the same pages, so a link or a bookmark keeps working. An administrator chooses for the whole organisation.": "",
  "Open Advanced in the sidebar footer. As an administrator, switch Full menu on. Or open Admin settings and go to Menu structure.": "",
  "Choose Full: every entry in the menu, as it was before. Simple brings the short menu back, with the modules you tick.": "",
  "The choice counts for everyone and shows the next time somebody opens Pipelinq. A page that is already open keeps its menu until then.": "",
